INT. LIGHTHOUSE LAMP ROOM - DAWN

Salt-streaked glass. A Fresnel lens the size of a bus shelter, still turning. Slow. Heavy.

IGNACIO, 30s, keeper's wool sweater, kneels at the brass base with an oilcan. Hands black with grease.

He hums. Off-key. Pleased with himself.

The hatch bangs.

He freezes. Listens.

Boots on iron stairs. Coming up.

IGNACIO
(muttering)
Supply boat's not till Friday.

The hatch lifts. A suitcase thumps onto the floor.

WREN, 30s, soaked to the bone, red scarf plastered to her neck, hauls herself up. Breathing hard. Grinning hard.

He stands. Oilcan still in hand.

IGNACIO (CONT'D)
No.

WREN
Hello to you too.

IGNACIO
You can't be here.

WREN
I rowed.

IGNACIO
You rowed. Eleven miles.

WREN
Nine. I cut the corner.

He sets the can down. Carefully. Like it might go off.

She drops her bag. Wrings out the scarf. Water pools on the floor.

IGNACIO
You wrote that you were done.

WREN
I wrote a lot of things.

IGNACIO
You wrote one letter. Four lines.

WREN
It was a good four lines.

He turns away. Faces the lens. It sweeps past, throwing fractured light across his face.

She watches. Doesn't close the gap.

WREN (CONT'D)
You kept the light on.

IGNACIO
It's a lighthouse.

WREN
You kept it polished.

IGNACIO
It's my job.

WREN
(softly)
Ignacio.

He doesn't answer. His shoulders drop an inch.

She crosses to the rail. Rain ticks against the glass. Far below, the sea is a gray animal, restless.

WREN (CONT'D)
I almost didn't make it. The boat took water by the rocks.

IGNACIO
You could have drowned.

WREN
I know.

IGNACIO
You could have drowned, and I'd have been up here. Oiling a gear.

She turns. Their eyes meet. Held.

WREN
Say it, then.

IGNACIO
Say what?

WREN
Whatever you've been rehearsing.

A beat. He shakes his head. A small, defeated laugh.

IGNACIO
It was better yesterday.

WREN
Try me.

IGNACIO
I missed you.

WREN ^
I missed you.

They say it on top of each other. Neither stops.

IGNACIO
I was angry. I'm still angry.

WREN
I was scared. I'm still scared.

They stop. Both laugh. Short. Wet.

IGNACIO
You're dripping on my floor.

WREN
You're welcome.

He picks up a towel from a hook. Tosses it. She catches it one-handed.

She dries her face. Her hands. She's slowing down.

WREN (CONT'D)
Is there tea?

IGNACIO
There's a kettle.

WREN
That's not what I asked.

IGNACIO
There's a kettle and a tin that might be tea.

WREN
Might be.

IGNACIO
It's been there since March.

WREN
Brave.

He crosses to the hatch. Stops. Looks down the shaft.

IGNACIO
Stairs are slick. Come on.

WREN
Is that an invitation?

IGNACIO
It's a warning.

She smiles. Picks up her suitcase. He takes it from her before she can protest.

They descend. His head vanishes first. Then hers.

The lens keeps turning. Light sweeps the empty room.
